<!-- start: FAQS Section -->
<section class="h6-project-section my-5 py-2">

  <div class="mx-5 px-5">
    <div class="shadowbox mx-5">
      <div class="sec-heading text-center pt-5">
        <span class="sub-title wow fadeInUp mt-5" data-wow-delay="0.1s">FAQ</span>
        <h2 class="sec-title text-anim">Legal Counsel Built Around Your Business</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col">
          <div class="h6-project-wrap">

            <!-- Item 01 — pinned (stacks/reveals as you scroll) -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">01.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">A Different Model for Ongoing Legal Counsel</h3>
                  <div class="desc">An ongoing legal relationship that brings continuity, context, and senior-level legal support to businesses as they grow, change, and evolve.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Item 02 — pinned -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">02.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">What is a Fractional General Counsel?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">A Fractional General Counsel is an ongoing legal counsel arrangement that gives a business access to senior-level legal advice and strategic support without appointing a full-time General Counsel. The counsel works with the business on a continuing basis, develops an understanding of its operations and priorities, and provides legal support as needs arise—without becoming part of the organisation’s payroll or adding the overhead associated with a full-time role.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Item 03 — pinned -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">03.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">How does the Fractional General Counsel model work?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">The relationship is ongoing, but the engagement is flexible. Rather than employing a full-time General Counsel, the business retains access to senior legal counsel who understands its context and provides support across its evolving legal needs. The business pays for the legal services and support actually required, based on the agreed engagement structure.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Item 04 — NOT pinned (final card, comes to rest naturally, same as
                 the original theme pattern where the last stack item has no pin class) -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">04.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">What value does a Fractional General Counsel bring to a business?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">The model provides continuity without the fixed commitment of a full-time legal leadership role. Over time, the counsel develops an understanding of the business, allowing legal advice to be more informed by its operations, priorities, and objectives. This gives the business access to ongoing senior legal support while keeping the engagement aligned with its actual legal needs.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Item 04 — NOT pinned (final card, comes to rest naturally, same as
                 the original theme pattern where the last stack item has no pin class) -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">05.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">Who can benefit from a Fractional General Counsel?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">The model can support founders, startups, SMEs, growth-stage and established businesses, international companies entering or expanding in India, and in-house legal teams that need additional senior-level legal capacity. It is particularly relevant for businesses that need an ongoing legal relationship and access to experienced counsel, but do not require or wish to add a full-time General Counsel to their organisation.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Item 04 — NOT pinned (final card, comes to rest naturally, same as
                 the original theme pattern where the last stack item has no pin class) -->
            <div class="h6-project-item approach-stack">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">06.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">When should a business consider a Fractional General Counsel?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">A business can engage a Fractional General Counsel from incorporation and at any stage of its growth. The support may range from addressing day-to-day legal queries and advising on important business communications to establishing legal and governance foundations, entering into commercial relationships, raising investment, expanding operations, entering new markets, managing organisational change, and navigating complex business decisions. The engagement evolves with the business, providing ongoing legal counsel aligned with its changing needs and priorities.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Item 04 — NOT pinned (final card, comes to rest naturally, same as
                 the original theme pattern where the last stack item has no pin class) -->
            <div class="h6-project-item">
              <div class="project_image">
                <img src="assets/images/vidhitra/approach/ap3.png" alt="We help leadership weigh the decision, not just the risk">
              </div>
              <div class="project_content">
                <div class="project_content_inner">
                  <span class="no">07.</span>
                  <h3 class="title">What role does a Fractional General Counsel play in a business?</h3>
                  <div class="desc">A Fractional General Counsel provides ongoing legal counsel that develops with the business. By understanding the organisation, its operations, priorities, and history, the counsel can support day-to-day legal queries, business communications, ongoing legal matters, and important business decisions with greater context. The model can also work alongside external law firms and in-house legal teams, providing additional senior-level capacity, business context, and continuity of legal support as and when required.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
